usage: build-fight-value.py [-h] [--states STATES] [--game-data GAME_DATA]
                            --character CHARACTER --rows ROWS [--out OUT]
                            [--notes NOTES] [--trees TREES] [--cutoff CUTOFF]
                            {opening-extract,opening-train}

Whole-fight opening-state predictor; separate labels/features from the turn
model. All card descriptors and encounter frequencies are observations, not
card values. The exported trees have the same strict-less-than evaluator in
Python and TS.

positional arguments:
  {opening-extract,opening-train}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --states STATES
  --game-data GAME_DATA
  --character CHARACTER
  --rows ROWS
  --out OUT
  --notes NOTES
  --trees TREES
  --cutoff CUTOFF       Exclude this timestamp and later from
                        fitting/calibration/test
